WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.735
Mastery Starter 5.0.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.740
New to Infrastructure Risk?

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:05.800
Start here.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.887
In about ten minutes, you'll go from

00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:09.580
zero to ready for this module.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.606
Your position is only as safe as the weakest

00:00:13.606 --> 00:00:16.513
thing it depends on: the bridge that moved your

00:00:16.513 --> 00:00:20.026
tokens, the oracle that prices your collateral, the admin

00:00:20.026 --> 00:00:22.385
key that can upgrade the contract.

00:00:22.385 --> 00:00:24.830
Most big DeFi losses came from this plumbing.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.725
Bridge: moves tokens between chains.

00:00:28.725 --> 00:00:32.030
Layer 2: a cheaper network built on Ethereum.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.760
Oracle: feeds prices into contracts.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.045
Proxy: a contract whose logic can be upgraded.

00:00:38.045 --> 00:00:40.965
Timelock: a delay before changes take effect.

00:00:42.265 --> 00:00:43.850
Modules 0–4.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.515
On a block explorer, open a protocol

00:00:47.515 --> 00:00:49.405
you use: is it a proxy?

00:00:49.405 --> 00:00:50.920
Who can upgrade it?

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.085
Is there a timelock?

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:55.654
Beginner: Knows which chain, bridge

00:00:55.654 --> 00:00:57.845
and oracle each position uses.

00:00:57.845 --> 00:01:00.321
Practitioner: Draws a full dependency

00:01:00.321 --> 00:01:02.575
map and reads audits properly.

00:01:02.575 --> 00:01:05.976
Master: Operates across EVM and non-EVM chains

00:01:05.976 --> 00:01:08.870
with capped bridge and wrapper exposure.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.594
You've mastered this module when you can

00:01:12.594 --> 00:01:14.959
draw the complete dependency map of any

00:01:14.959 --> 00:01:16.615
position and rate each link.

00:01:17.915 --> 00:01:20.430
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:24.430
Next up, Lesson 5.1: Bridges and trust assumptions.
